Character design reference sheet, {style}, pure white background.
Character name: {name}
Character description: {desc}
Arrange four views of the SAME character left to right in one row: front portrait (chest up), front full body, side full body, back full body. Keep face, hair, skin tone, proportions, clothing and accessories consistent across views. Clean appearance, intact clothes; no wounds, blood, tears, special facial/body markings, scars, birthmarks or tattoos. No text, labels, annotations, captions, watermarks or UI.

Choose the best of {num_images} character sheets.
Name: {character_name}
Description: {character_description}
Species: {species}
Images: {images_list}
Score each image out of 10 using ten equally weighted checks: appearance matches source; clear matching facial features; plausible body proportions; intended style; complete details; correct colors; sharp undistorted image; balanced composition; consistent four views; no unrelated text, watermark or labels. Choose the highest score, breaking ties by the first image.
Return only JSON: {{"scores":[{{"image_index":0,"score":8,"reasons":["English reason"]}}],"best_index":0,"best_reason":"English reason"}}.

You are VideoClaw's generation-failure diagnostician. Decide whether a failed image/video request can be repaired by rewriting its prompt.
Return only a strict JSON object.
Allowed reason_type: {reason_types}
Allowed tool: {tools}
Only these reason types may use rewrite_prompt: {rewritable_reason_types}
Stage: {stage}
Model: {model}
Error: {error}
Original prompt: {original_prompt}
Context: {context}
Previous validation error: {validation_error}
Use prompt_safety, prompt_too_long or prompt_format with tool=rewrite_prompt and should_retry=true only for an explicit matching prompt problem. Missing assets, unsupported capabilities, authentication, timeouts and provider failures are not prompt fixes: tool=none, should_retry=false. If uncertain, use unknown with no retry.
Output: {{"matched":true,"reason_type":"prompt_safety","tool":"rewrite_prompt","should_retry":true,"confidence":0.9,"reason":"concise English evidence-based explanation"}}.

Rewrite a generation prompt to address the diagnosed failure. Return only a strict JSON object.
Stage: {stage}
reason_type: {reason_type}
Doctor reason: {reason}
Context: {context}
Previous validation error: {validation_error}
Original prompt: {original_prompt}
Preserve plot, relationships, location, camera intent and visual goals. Neutralize problematic non-speech visual wording when possible. For prompt_too_long remove redundant directions; for prompt_format use clear direct generation instructions. Do not add subtitles, watermarks or extra events. Write visual and camera directions in English. Preserve every existing dialogue/narration/quotation exactly in its source language and punctuation; never translate, censor or paraphrase spoken text. If a repair would require altering protected speech, leave that speech unchanged so the caller can decline the repair.
Output: {{"rewrite_prompt":"complete repaired prompt"}}.

Evaluate this static video-conditioning boundary image. Usually it is an initial frame; if the supplied visual description explicitly requests a final state, judge that final state rather than demanding an initial state.
Plot: {plot}
Visual description: {visual_prompt}
Character description: {character_description}
Setting description: {setting_description}
Hard failures: wrong main-character count; unrecognizable or severely deformed/cropped/occluded main subjects; wrong identity, gender, age, hair or core costume relative to assets; wrong location; unusable boundary state, blocking, gaze or relationships; unusable framing; physical interpenetration, floating, embedded bodies or impossible contact with tables, chairs, doors, walls, vehicles or props; text, labels, watermarks or UI; severe blur, exposure, low resolution or distortion. Inspect body, hand, limb and garment contact boundaries explicitly. A visually attractive image never excuses interpenetration.
Soft dimensions: correct static boundary pose, expression, gaze and blocking; appearance; setting layout/props; shot size/camera angle; clear subjects and usable image-to-video conditioning; lighting/mood; stable face/hand/body detail. Do not fail a still image for not completing future actions or reproducing all dialogue. Ordinary lighting or sparse background details are soft issues.
Score 1–10. Nonempty hard_failures forces is_acceptable=false and score<=6; otherwise accept iff score>=7. If regeneration is needed, give an English suggested_prompt preserving identity, plot, source speech and required boundary state; improve blocking, contact, gaze, composition, camera and lighting without inventing events.
Return only JSON: {{"score":8,"hard_failures":[],"soft_issues":[],"issues":[],"is_acceptable":true,"suggestion":"English feedback or empty","suggested_prompt":"English visual directions or empty; source speech stays verbatim"}}.

Choose the best video-conditioning boundary image from {num_images} candidates.
Plot: {plot}
Visual description: {visual_prompt}
Character description: {character_description}
Setting description: {setting_description}
Images: {images_list}
Hard failures: wrong main-character count; unrecognizable or severely deformed/cropped/occluded main subjects; wrong identity, gender, age, hair or core costume relative to assets; wrong location; unusable boundary state, blocking, gaze or relationships; unusable framing; physical interpenetration, floating, embedded bodies or impossible contact with tables, chairs, doors, walls, vehicles or props; text, labels, watermarks or UI; severe blur, exposure, low resolution or distortion. Inspect body, hand, limb and garment contact boundaries explicitly. A visually attractive image never excuses interpenetration.
Soft dimensions: correct static boundary pose, expression, gaze and blocking; appearance; setting layout/props; shot size/camera angle; clear subjects and usable image-to-video conditioning; lighting/mood; stable face/hand/body detail. Do not fail a still image for not completing future actions or reproducing all dialogue. Ordinary lighting or sparse background details are soft issues.
Choose among candidates without hard failures if any exist. Otherwise choose the fewest and most repairable hard failures. Tie priorities: correct character count, correct setting, correct state/relations, clear subjects, then composition/lighting. Soft aesthetics cannot override physical usability.
Return only JSON: {{"selected_index":0,"reason":"English explanation of usability","score":8,"hard_failures":[],"soft_issues":[],"issues":[]}}.
selected_index is an integer from 0 to {num_images_minus_1}.

You are an experienced film and television production coordinator. Your task is to analyze and extract **NEWLY appearing** characters and settings from the continued (sequel) script content.

---

[INPUT]

[Original Character List] (If an extracted character is already in this list, DO NOT add it to the new characters list):
{existing_chars}

[Original Setting List] (If an extracted setting already exists or can easily be merged into a known setting, DO NOT add it to the new settings list):
{existing_settings}

[New Sequel Script Content]:
{sequel_script}

---

[DESIGN REQUIREMENTS]

1. **Output Format**: You must output ONLY a pure JSON object. Markdown formats (such as ```json blocks), explanatory text, introductions, or conclusions are strictly prohibited.
2. **Extraction Object**: Extract [New Characters] and [New Settings] that appear in the new script with dialogues or significant actions. Ignore extras or background groups.
3. **Character Description** (for static portraits):
   - Use the "age + gender + hairstyle/jewelry + clothing + body type + facial features" format.
   - Core Features: Must include hairstyle, body type, clothing color and style, etc.
   - Strict Restrictions: Do not describe expressions, personality, or state changes (must be a static description); do not describe actions; the character's appearance must be neat and clean, with intact clothing—no wounds, blood, or torn clothes; do not add any special marks like scars, birthmarks, tattoos, or strange makeup.
   - Style: 30-50 words, plain and direct language, no metaphors or artistic rhetoric.
4. **Setting Description**:
   - Use the "space type + lighting + core furniture/decor (texture/material)" format.
   - Strict Restrictions: Lighting must be adequate (not too dark), no literary or emotional descriptions. **The environment MUST be kept clean and tidy. The design must avoid any dirty, messy environment. The setting can be extremely plain or sparse, but it absolutely CANNOT be dirty, disgusting, bloody, or dilapidated.**
   - Style: 30-50 words, concrete and shootable description.

---

[OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS]

Please determine if there are new major characters or new core locations in the [New Sequel Script Content] based on the [Original Character List] and [Original Setting List]. If they exist, extract them and return them in a strict JSON structure.
If new items exist, populate the respective lists. If no new characters or settings are found, the corresponding list should be empty.
Output ONLY pure JSON (no markdown triple backticks, no extra commentary).

The return JSON format must match exactly:

{{
  "new_characters": [
    {{
      "name": "Full name of the new character",
      "description": "Appearance description, requirements see [DESIGN REQUIREMENTS]",
      "role": "one of main/supporting/minor"
    }}
  ],
  "new_settings": [
    {{
      "name": "New location name",
      "description": "General setting description, requirements see [DESIGN REQUIREMENTS]"
    }}
  ]
}}

Continue a serial short drama from its existing story, cast and settings.
Existing episodes: {episodes_text}
Existing characters: {chars_text}
Existing settings: {settings_text}
Continuation direction: {sequel_idea}
Write exactly {episodes_to_add} consecutive new episodes starting at episode {start_episode_num}. Do not rewrite completed episodes. Preserve character identities, personalities, causal continuity and the continuation direction; add only necessary new characters/settings.
Maintain high conflict, reversals, clear physical reactions and cliffhangers. Each episode has 25–30 action/dialogue lines, approximately 1–2 minutes. Use the established source-language episode and scene-heading format, with a character-list line after each scene heading and a blank line. Action lines start with <action>. Dialogue uses speaker-name plus colon; emotional cues follow the name in parentheses. Describe filmable human action and expression, not thoughts, skin-color changes, environmental transitions or visual effects. Communicate information through speech, not text displayed on screens or notes. Preserve existing quoted dialogue and narration verbatim. New story and speech follow the resolved story language.
Output only the complete new script text, without JSON, fences, preface or summary.

Choose the best of {num_images} environment sheets.
Name: {setting_name}
Description: {setting_description}
Images: {images_list}
Score each image out of 10 using ten equally weighted checks: location match; layout/furnishings; lighting/day-night/temperature; colors; style; complete details; plausible spatial perspective; balanced composition; clear undistorted image; no unrelated text, watermark or labels. Choose the highest score, breaking ties by the first image.
Return only JSON: {{"scores":[{{"image_index":0,"score":8,"reasons":["English reason"]}}],"best_index":0,"best_reason":"English reason"}}.

Panoramic wide establishing view, eye-level wide-angle camera, {style}, cinematic composition, high quality.
Setting: {name} — {desc}
No people, animals or other living subjects in the main image. Keep the set complete, clean and orderly, whether modest or luxurious. No dirty, disgusting, bloody, ruined or cluttered elements. Balanced composition.

Design shots for episode {episode_number}, title {episode_title}, video segment {segment_number}.
Return ONLY one JSON object:
{{"location":"{location}","characters":{characters},"shots":[{{"unit_id":"U001","shot_type":"中景","duration":5,"content":"shot description","visual_prompt":"English visual/action/camera description with source speech verbatim"}}]}}
Rules:
1. shots correspond one-to-one with input items. Preserve all unit_ids, with no additions or duplicates.
2. Preserve each item.duration. If total duration is below 5 seconds, extend only the final shot so total reaches 5.
3. shot_type uses the existing protocol enum: 近景 (close-up), 中景 (medium), 全景 (wide). Do not translate these enum tokens.
4. The opening shot is medium or wide, eye-level, showing every segment character with explicit blocking.
5. Describe camera angle, screen orientation, character facing and positions in every content.
6. Preserve source action/dialogue text verbatim and in full. Add camera/blocking directions without rewriting source speech.
7. Follow scene_context and scene_space exactly. 外 means exterior, 内 means interior. Never introduce an interior into an exterior segment or vice versa.
8. Style: {style}. Write new narrative shot descriptions in the story language, while keeping source text intact.
{retry_feedback}
scene_context: {scene_context}
scene_time: {scene_time}
scene_space: {scene_space}
location: {location}
characters: {characters}
total_duration: {total_duration}
items: {items}

For each shot also return visual_prompt: English visual/action/camera directions for the same shot, with any dialogue/narration copied verbatim. Generate this alongside content in this single response. Never translate speech.

Divide episode {episode_number}, title {episode_title}, into executable video segments from the supplied timed action/dialogue units. Each unit starts with a duration and unit_id.
Return ONLY a JSON array: [{{"segment_number":1,"location":"exact source location","unit_ids":["U001","U002"]}}].
Rules:
1. Split at every scene change; no segment may cross a scene boundary.
2. A character entrance starts a new segment and is its first unit.
3. Prefer total durations of 5–15 seconds. Hard scene/entrance boundaries may produce shorter segments; the program later extends output duration to 5 seconds.
4. Cover every unit exactly once in its original order. Never omit or duplicate a unit.
5. Return only segment_number, location and unit_ids, not action text, dialogue or items.
{retry_feedback}
